  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Among the following compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo></math> which one forms a yellow precipitate on reacting sequentially with (i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> (ii) dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> (iii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0102_435f7b642596.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Only in&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0102_cdd0a898513c.png\" style=\"width: 149px; height: 107px;\" />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;can be substituted by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;combine with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;to form a yellow precipitate&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgI</mi></math>. While</p><p>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>II</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> substitution reaction is not possible due to partial double bond character.</p>"
  }
